{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1382683-need-help-with-a-mystery","id":1382683,"title":"Need Help With a Mystery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-19T23:01:07-07:00","id":1382683,"title":"Need Help With a Mystery","content":"So I'm getting ready to run my first Mage game in nearly 10 years. With the increased focus on mysteries in the second edition I wanted to take some things that were just there in my previous Mage game and put some of this stuff behind it.<br /> <br /> In the game I'm running I have an Revolutionary Girl Utena homage of an immortal person whose &quot;ownership&quot; is traded through duels.<br /> <br /> The player who currently is the winner of said tools wants to try to solve the mystery of what create this &quot;Bride&quot; and try to restore there free will and break whatever magical ties is keeping this person from being normal. <br /> <br /> In my mind, the spells used were arch mastery spells (unfortunately Imperial Mysteries came out when I wasn't running any games so I don't have it) So I call upon you all for help.<br /> <br /> The spells used to make the Bride makes them ageless, compelled to serve the orders of the person who &quot;possesses&quot; them, and changes who possesses them by ritual combat.<br /> <br /> There are other details and reasons for why someone did this but those are three big magical effects.<br /> <br /> What levels of Arcanum would have been necessary to pull this off? What sort of Opacity would it be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T04:34:56-07:00","id":1382712,"title":"","content":"Lets see, agelessness could be Veil of Moments, a spell to make something else age for them (Weaving of Time or Death), a Life spell to make new cells be at their prime, etc. There are lots of ways.<br /> <br /> Sworn Oaths for the ownership effect, or a Patterning to force it upon her. You could also use a Prime, Mind or Fate effect to overwrite her Obsession into the terms of the curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T05:53:31-07:00","id":1382726,"title":"","content":"The bride could be a spirit, as they are ageless, with multiple bans to explain her bejaviour.<br /> A level 7 spirit spell could made her permanently manifested and able to bear human children if needed, and set the owner as Resonant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T06:30:35-07:00","id":1382735,"title":"","content":"Since you mention archmastery, another possibility is that the Bride is under the influence of an Ananke. Maybe she <i>is </i>an Ananke, although her non-human nature would be obvious to Mage Sight. An Ananke is the creation of an archmaster of Fate or Time using the Practice of Dominions (which requires 8 dots in the Arcana).<br /> <br /> Ananke are described in Signs of Sorcery (page 116).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9493-enmai","name":"Enmai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T19:27:19-07:00","id":1382877,"title":"","content":"The Bride could herself be an archmaster whose long period of servitude (along with other ultimately self-imposed restrictions) functions as a yantra for a cosmically-powerful spell that the archmaster will cast once her servitude finally ends. Perhaps when the players solve her mystery she'll finally be prepared to carry out her plan.<br /> <br /> If you go this route you don't need to fuss with the limitations of standard Awakened magic; you can just make shit up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T10:44:02-07:00","id":1383165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1382683-need-help-with-a-mystery?p=1382877#post1382877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bride could herself be an archmaster whose long period of servitude (along with other ultimately self-imposed restrictions) functions as a yantra for a cosmically-powerful spell that the archmaster will cast once her servitude finally ends. Perhaps when the players solve her mystery she'll finally be prepared to carry out her plan.<br /> <br /> If you go this route you don't need to fuss with the limitations of standard Awakened magic; you can just make shit up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... Is a very interesting idea. And could potentially work really well with the original source of the idea that I took this from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2704,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","user":"DeimosMasque","date":".  Added more 04-22-2020, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T00:20:51-07:00","id":1384590,"title":"","content":"Mind 6 could simply render the target's will subordinate to whoever has the &quot;right&quot; to control her. Dynamics is certainly sufficient.<br /> Death, Life, or Time 7 could simply remove the applicability of death and decay from the target indefinitely.<br /> <br /> Since 2e, you no longer need archmastery to permanently apply spells, so an indefinite <b>Veil of Moments</b> wouldn't even require archmastery. Only throw in the Reach to Advanced Duration and to be able to heal. That means you wouldn't even need to master Time. 3 would suffice. (2 if Paradox risk isn't a barrier) (and the target would never regain willpower through normal means) <b>Psychic Reprogramming</b> might suffice to do the control, especially with willpower frozen. That's more arguable but would only require Mind 4.<br /> <br /> If that is sufficient to your desire, the biggest advantage to using an archmaster is the automatic winning of Clash of Wills tests against lesser magi.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":".  Correcting math and grammar 04-29-2020, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}